<title>UK: UK notes in circulation rise adjusted 5.4 pct.</title>
<headline>UK notes in circulation rise adjusted 5.4 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose an adjusted 5.4 percent in the week to December 18 over the equivalent year-ago week, the Bank of England said. Last week the annual adjusted rise was 5.8 percent.</p>
<p>NOTES IN CIRCULATION (in rounded bln stg) -</p>
<p>				Latest week  pvs week</p>
<p> Notes in circulation     22.41	   21.60</p>
<p> Bankers' deposits	   2.02	    1.95</p>
